RESMASK  DC    A(PAGPFRM)     MASK FOR PAGE RESIDENT           XA0036DK         
./ R 00854000          $ 00854100 100                                           
CLCNTINV DC    A(SEGPTOM)     CLEAR COUNT, INVALID &           XA0036DK         
./ R 00860000          $ 00860100 100                                           
*  PAGREF MOVED FROM BYTE 1 TO BYTE 3, SO THIS MASK IS         XA0036DK         
*  DERIVED FROM PAGREF RATHER THAN WRITTEN OUT. IT WAS         XA0036DK         
*  X'0000FFFE'.                                                XA0036DK         
REFMASK  DC    A(X'FFFFFFFF'-PAGREF) FORCE REF BIT OFF         XA0036DK         
./ R 00860500          $ 00860600 100                                           
INVLPTE  DC    A(PAGINVW)     INVALID PTE BIT MASK             XA0036DK         
./ R 00861000          $ 00861100 100                                           
*  SWLENGTH WAS DC F'192' -- A HARD-CODED PAGBMP, IN THIS      XA0036DK         
*  MODULE AND IN DMKVMA, WITH NOTHING JOINING IT TO            XA0036DK         
*  CORE.COPY. I-116'S SHAPE.                                   XA0036DK         
SWLENGTH DC    A(PAGBMP)      LENGTH OF SHARED PAGE &          XA0036DK         
./ R 00863000 00864000 $ 00863100 100                                           
*  FORCEPG0 WAS X'00FF0000', THE 64 KB SEGMENT NUMBER IN BITS  XA0036DK         
*  8-15, WHICH IS EVERY SEGMENT A 24-BIT ADDRESS CAN NAME. A   XA0036DK         
*  1 MB SEGMENT NUMBER IS BITS 1-11, SO THE MASK THAT LEAVES   XA0036DK         
*  A SEGMENT START IS X'7FF00000' -- DMKVAT'S OWN CODEB0       XA0036DK         
*  VALUE, AND THE SAME ONE DMKPGS 01049300 AND 01054000        XA0036DK         
*  CARRY. I-188.                                               XA0036DK         
*  FORCEPGF WAS X'0000F000', PAGE 15, THE LAST OF A 64 KB      XA0036DK         
*  SEGMENT'S SIXTEEN. A 1 MB SEGMENT HAS 256 PAGES AND ITS     XA0036DK         
*  LAST IS 255, SO THE MASK IS X'000FF000'. 00343000 ANDS      XA0036DK         
*  WITH THIS SAME CONSTANT TO GET A PAGE NUMBER -- BITS 12-19  XA0036DK         
*  NOW, NOT 16-19 -- AND THE SRL 9 THAT FOLLOWS IT STAYS: IT   XA0036DK         
*  RELATES A PAGE'S ADDRESS WEIGHT OF 4096 TO AN 8-BYTE        XA0036DK         
*  SWPTABLE ENTRY, AND NEITHER MOVED.                          XA0036DK         
FORCEPG0 DC    X'7FF00000'    MASK FOR SEGMENT & PAGE 0        XA0036DK         
FORCEPGF DC    X'000FF000'    MASK FOR LAST PAGE OF SEGMENT    XA0036DK         
